  "body": "Part of #4023. It is delivered on `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**). It does not depend on the crate skeleton (#4055, PR #4123): it adds tests and recorded files only.\n\n## Why\n\nThe switch-over proof of the record `docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md` compares the old planners with the new kernel for the 16 kinds of phase 1. The baseline of #3750 (commit `9c69f004a`) records only 2D Offset, the 2D Pocket rings and the level rings. PR #4123 says that 2D Pocket has no app-level golden. The other kinds have no recorded baseline for this comparison.\n\n## What to do\n\nRecord the output of the OLD planners, on the unchanged code of the side branch, for each phase-1 kind that has no baseline: Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket (app level), 2D Adaptive, Engrave, V-Carve, 2D Chamfer, Circular, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Trace, Slot Undercut, Thread, Bore and 3D Pocket.\n\n- Use the same form as the #3750 baseline (`shared_planner.rs` pins and their golden files): the toolpath at 1 um, with the notes and the verifier warnings.\n- For each kind, record a small set of cases that covers its strategies and its start sides: for example Inside and Outside, each entry kind, with and without stock. Use the existing fixtures (the disc, the dog bone, `fig8.step` where a kind already uses it). Keep each case under the 60 s debug budget, or put it in the heavy lane with its light twin by the rules.\n- Each pin runs with the planner switch at its default. The pins must be green on the unchanged code. Change no planner code and no existing golden.\n- Add the pins to existing directory suites.\n\n## Done means\n\nEach of the 16 kinds has a recorded baseline of the old planner, the pins are green on the side branch, and a table in the PR body lists each kind, its cases and its golden files (`Goldens moved`: additions only).\n",
